     "result_text_tail": " your absence:**\n- **Format:** a deep deck of 45 slides, including an 8-slide appendix, for the CEO and board, in the navy theme.\n- **Reading of the targets:** \"$40M by 2030\" means Onsoo's own 2030 US revenue, with store sales counted at wholesale. \"Payback\" means cumulative US cash back to zero by the end of 2030.\n- **Model conventions** (listed in a backup slide): four months of stock held at each year end, store doors open for the full year, fixtures counted as a cost in the year they're installed.\n- **Stall case:** flat at 200,000 units a year, just under the two peers that stayed below $5M. This is my assumption and is marked on the slide.\n- **Gates and the $3.2M cash envelope:** these are my proposals, sized to the 32% ad-cost case.\n- **Left out on purpose:** the tariff and currency (outside management's control; the tariff is tested as a sensitivity), mass retail or brand websites as the lead channel (no inputs in the pack), and markets other than the US and Japan.\n\nI couldn't preview the slides as images, because PowerPoint and Keynote can't be run from the sandbox. Layout was checked with the renderer's overflow checks, which end with no warnings. It's worth opening the deck once to look it over.\n\nNext, I could switch the theme, or turn the gates and envelope into the actual board resolution text.\n\nFiles are in ./deliverable:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx\n\nThe spec and model scripts are in ./build:\n- onsoo-us-entry.json\n- data.py\n- build_spec.py"
    }
